                    "text": "The Rural Health Transformation Program is a critical step toward stabilizing rural healthcare\u2014finally prioritizing communities over bureaucracy. By allocating $50 billion through the Working Families Tax Cut Act, the administration is addressing systemic failures that left rural hospitals collapsing under outdated payment models and regulatory bloat.\n\nThe program\u2019s focus on sustainable alliances, tech innovation, and workforce retention (as outlined in H.R. 3684) directly tackles the 60% occupancy crisis and chronic underfunding that shuttered 151 facilities since 2010.\n\nThis isn\u2019t just funding\u2014it\u2019s a structural overhaul to prevent closures, streamline services, and align incentives with outcomes, not just urban-centric metrics. Real progress, not performative spending.",
